Australian Product Guide — National-grade platform current release record
Release date: 2026-08-17
Production source: GitHub main via Vercel
Canonical production domain: https://australianproductguide.au

Current platform: institutional v9 consumer design and navigation, v11 footer, Decision Lab / explainable recommendation journeys, My APG local-first workspace with optional account sync, universal search, comparison, category/product/guide/trust surfaces, responsive accessibility hardening, privacy-first analytics consent and Amazon Associates controls. Architecture remains lightweight SSR-first Node with progressive enhancement.

Catalogue truth: 257 maintained products; 48 populated categories; 112 brands; 37 deep-evidence products; 220 starter-evidence products. Starter records are explicitly labelled and are not represented as equivalent to deep research.

Amazon Australia retailer truth: 22 verified exact product destinations and 235 model-specific search/further-verification fallbacks across the 257 maintained products. Exact links require verified product/model identity and an observed Amazon Australia detail page; no ASIN is guessed. Eligible affiliate destinations use tag auproductguid-22. Retailer/affiliate availability and commission contribute zero recommendation points.

Imagery truth: exact external product photography is not claimed unless rights and model identity are verified. APG-authored semantic/product-category illustrations remain the controlled fallback where authorised exact photography is unavailable.

Privacy/analytics: Google Analytics is opt-in. Analytics storage defaults to denied and the GA script is loaded only after the visitor allows analytics. Essential browser storage remains available for privacy preferences and core/local-first research functionality. Account creation is optional and does not affect recommendations.

Current release changes: mobile shopping-assistant entry point is reduced to a safe-area-aware icon on small screens to avoid obscuring decision content; two newly verified exact Amazon Australia destinations were added for Anker Nano Power Bank 10,000mAh 30W (A1259) and INIU Power Bank 20,000mAh 45W (P51L). Existing privacy-consent and accessibility/performance changes were preserved during a clean rebase onto the latest main branch.

Release discipline: GitHub main is authoritative; Vercel Production must match the current source SHA; public canonical pages, retailer links, SEO/trust surfaces and responsive behaviour must be verified before the release is treated as complete. Historical v7 release counts and deployment identifiers are superseded by this record.
